## Overview

A wonderful panoramic hike in the mountains of Central Switzerland.
Not particularly challenging, as it is mostly flat or gently downhill.
Unfortunately, the weather wasn’t entirely on our side during our visit, which is why large sections were shrouded in mist.

## How to get there

Journey via Altdorf, Uri and then by bus to the Klausen Pass.
<JourneyPlanner from="<current location>" to="Klausen Passhöhe" toFixed time="09:00" target="arrival" />

The hike got off to a wonderful start with a sweeping view across the valley.
<HikeImage idx={0} />

We also came across a mountain newt straight away.
<HikeImage idx={1} />
<HikeImage idx={2} />
<HikeImage idx={3} />
<HikeImage idx={4} />
<HikeImage idx={5} />
<HikeImage idx={6} />

Just before the mist rolled in, we still had a wonderful view of the Gross Windgällen (on the right) and the Gross Ruchen (on the left)
<HikeImage idx={7} />
<HikeImage idx={8} />
<HikeImage idx={9} />
<HikeImage idx={10} />
Unfortunately, after 1.5 hours, the fog set in, which made it difficult to enjoy the view.
Nevertheless, the hike offered a lovely trail.
<HikeImage idx={11} />
<HikeImage idx={12} />
<HikeImage idx={13} />
<HikeImage idx={14} />
<HikeImage idx={15} />
<HikeImage idx={16} />

In the Mättental valley, there were several opportunities to buy mountain cheese directly from the farm. A lovely souvenir from the hike.
<HikeImage idx={17} />
After about 4 hours, the fog had largely cleared and we were able to enjoy the beautiful Alpine landscape.
